Subject: [PATCH] t214: save and restore SC7 CAR clock context

Apply after 0007-t214-bpmp-sc7-prepare.patch. Enabled only when
SWITCH_LITE_SC7=1 on T210B01.

Save and restore non-DRAM CAR PLLs, glitchless open-loop CCLK_BURST_POLICY /
SUPER_CCLK_DIVIDER (parking CCLK on CLK_M if warmboot left PLLX running at a
boot divider), system bus dividers, peripheral clock sources, resets, and
clock gates at the last-CPU SC7 boundary before non-secure drivers resume.
Leave PLLM/PLLP/EMC ownership to warmboot/BPMP.

References:
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra210.c
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-tegra210b01.c
https://github.com/CTCaer/switch-l4t-kernel-4.9/blob/2d0059fd3167a8df756de2aa0489d4aa70a9fc15/drivers/clk/tegra/clk-pll.c

